# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every `target/` at any depth: the workspace's own, and the one each example
# and generated Rust crate creates next to itself. This one rule replaces the
# ~20 hand-added per-example paths that used to live here -- a new example
# should never require a new ignore entry.
target/
Cargo.lock.bak
*.rs.bk

# Compiler-generated foreign-crate stub caches (`rust.<crate>` deps).
# Regenerated on build; never checked in.
.jux-stubs/

# Throwaway binaries some workflows drop at the repo root. The real build
# output is target/release/.
/juxc.exe
/jux.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.stackdump

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local working files (not part of the project)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI-tooling and scratch notes stay out of the published tree.
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
/TODO.md
/next-session.md
/optimizations.md
/classes-rules.md
/crm.html
/out.txt
/stdout.txt
/stderr.txt
# Redirect files from launching a demo binary, at any depth.
out.txt
err.txt
/graphify-out/
/ref-only/
_bugtest/
/tmp_bughunt/

# Requests exchanged with the IDE-plugin work; local coordination, not product.
/ide/request.md
/ide/bug-request-generics.md
/ide/intellij-plugin/cli-support-request.md

# The Gradle wrapper itself IS checked in (INSTALL.md tells users to run
# `./gradlew buildPlugin`, which needs it) -- only Gradle's own caches are not.
/ide/intellij-plugin/.gradle/
